 g=read(E/'amended_gate_decision.json');r=read(E/'panel_release_receipt.json');t=read(E/'amendment_timeline.json');facts=read(E/'evidence_reassessment.json')['facts'];p=read(E/'amended_source_validation_protocol.json')
 text=f'''# Stage 3B — Prospective Protocol Amendment & Source-Gate Re-release\n\n**{g['classification']}**. Future Part B authorized: **{g['part_b_authorized']}**. No Part B scientific code executed.\n\n## 1. Historical audit chain\n\n| Record | Date / UTC time | Permanent interpretation |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Original Stage 3 protocol | {t['original_protocol']['timestamp']} | Original frozen validation rule |\n| Stage 3 failed build receipt | {t['stage3_failure']['verified_build_at']} | BLOCKED under original MIN rule |\n| Stage 3A precision decision | {t['stage3a_audit']['decision_at']} | UNRESOLVED — INSUFFICIENT PRECISION EVIDENCE |\n| Stage 3B amendment frozen | {p['frozen_at']} | New prospective field-specific rule |\n| Stage 3B gate reassessed | {g['evaluated_at']} | {g['classification']} |\n\nThe original protocol lacks an embedded timestamp: its date/time above comes from filesystem birth metadata, with the dated original build receipt as an independent upper bound. The failure timestamp identifies the preserved blocked build, not necessarily the first failure instant. No historical file has been relabeled or overwritten. Stage 3A remains unresolved under its mechanism-demonstration prerequisite. Stage 3B explicitly changes that prerequisite for future release; it does not claim to have satisfied it retrospectively.\n\nThis amendment is **prospective to scientific inference, after validation discrepancies were known**. It is not described as pre-data registration. No Stage 3 hierarchical estimate, beta_RW, posterior, p-value, or association result exists at amendment time. Prior Stage 1/2 development analyses remain historical and are not represented as absent.\n\n## 2. Why the original MIN gate failed\n\nFour predeclared sample comparisons and 170 census comparisons exceeded the original season-decimal MIN rule. The original rule remains failed. Stage 3B introduces no numerical replacement threshold, substitutes no official totals, changes no observations, and removes no discrepant players.\n\n## 3. What Stage 3A established\n\nReassessment reads preserved row-level records and raw official DOM captures; it does not merely copy report conclusions. Source checksums are verified against prior manifests. Findings:\n\n- All 7,550 player comparisons for FTM, FTA, 3PM, 3PA and GP are exact, including 3,020 FTM/FTA comparisons. All 450 team comparisons are exact.\n- All 53 audited player-seasons and 2,861 recorded appearances have exactly matching archived and official displayed game MIN strings. Dates, regular-season game IDs and complete recorded-appearance sets agree.\n- Official season GP equals reconstructed official and archive recorded GP in every audited player-season.\n- All 1,510 official/archive season-pair comparisons agree on positive-minute eligibility, including all 170 season-display mismatches; the 53 game reconstructions also agree.\n- All 15 archive-directed recorded 0:00 cases are confirmed. Rakeem Christmas on 2017-04-10, game 0021601203, is officially 0:00 with 1 FTM and 2 FTA.\n- Available game-level displays show no archive-versus-official minute disagreement. In the four original cases, summing NBA game displays reproduces the archive total while differing from NBA season decimals.\n\nThe 698 archive empty/DNP rows absent from appearance-only official logs retain **missing official evidence**, not inferred official DNP or zero. Explicit independent DNP/DND corroboration covers 26 rows in the Christmas box score. Zero-minute sampling was archive-directed; game logs were audited for 53 player-seasons, not every league player-season. These scope limitations remain operative.\n\n## 4. What remains unresolved\n\nNBA's internal season-minute aggregation algorithm is unknown. Whole-second public displays may represent finer underlying clocks. The 170-mismatch distribution is asymmetric (157 positive, 13 negative). Neither a simple rounding rule nor a truncation rule is proved; no claim is made that exact true playing time was recovered or archive season minutes equal hidden official raw minutes. This unresolved representation issue is retained rather than relabeled resolved.\n\n## 5. Variable-role distinction\n\nThe response is **FTM out of FTA**. Relevant primary inputs are FTM, FTA, residual wingspan, barefoot height, combine position, season and player identity. Exact response counts are essential to the likelihood. Correct player-season eligibility determines panel membership. MIN does not define the response, exposure, primary predictor or beta-binomial count likelihood; it defines positive-time eligibility and supplies descriptive coverage summaries.\n\nValidation therefore separates scientific counts, playing-time classification, and season-display reconciliation. Directly corroborated game records and unchanged membership support a prospective field-specific rule without knowing how NBA generates a separate season-minute display. The amendment's justification is this semantic role and observable evidence, **not the magnitude of the discrepancies**.\n\n## 6. New prospective validation rule\n\nA. **Primary counts:** FTM, FTA, 3PM, 3PA and GP must match exactly in the official validation samples/censuses. Unexplained FTM or FTA disagreement blocks inference.\n\nB. **Audited game records:** Player, season, game identity/date, recorded appearance sets and displayed MM:SS must reconcile at the finest successfully retrieved official precision. Any unexplained game disagreement blocks release. Recorded 0:00 stays distinct from empty/missing/DNP. No unobserved finer-clock precision is claimed.\n\nC. **Eligibility:** Positive-total-time player-season eligibility must agree. For an eligible season, aggregate all recorded appearances, including 0:00. Empty/DNP rows are never converted to zero-time appearances. Any eligibility-changing disagreement blocks release.\n\nD. **Season decimal MIN:** Retain and audit as an ancillary representation. Equality between summed displayed game MM:SS and official season decimal MIN is not a release gate when exact primary counts, reconciled audited appearances and available game displays, preserved positive/zero/missing-DNP distinctions, and unchanged eligibility all hold. No numerical tolerance is introduced. An unknown internal mechanism remains a limitation.\n\nLater measurement validation, quarantine, unchanged candidate hashes, and absence of Stage 3 scientific analysis before adoption remain mandatory. The scope is the same collected official census and game audit; no observation was recollected or selectively replaced. Frozen specification: `stage3b_evidence/amended_source_validation_protocol.json`, SHA256 `{sha(E/'amended_source_validation_protocol.json')}`.\n\n## 7. Why no numeric tolerance is introduced\n\nThe rule changes which representation is relevant to release, conditional on count, appearance and eligibility validation. It neither chooses an allowance from the observed maximum nor increases the old cutoff. Season decimal discrepancies remain visible in their unchanged original ledgers. Known magnitudes are not input to the gate-decision function. The protocol explicitly sets numerical MIN tolerance to null.\n\n## 8. Reassessment under amended protocol\n\n'''
 text+='| Required condition | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n'+'\n'.join(f'| {k.replace("_"," ")} | {"PASS" if v else "FAIL"} |' for k,v in g['conditions'].items())+'\n'
 text+=f'''\nAll required conditions pass. Later anthropometric evidence covers 582 rows, 543 validated complete pairs and four official corrections; 39 incomplete/quarantined pairs remain outside the selected vectors. No unresolved quarantined pair was admitted. Preserved evidence hashes and {facts['preserved_files']} preexisting artifact hashes agree. `evidence_reassessment.json` records the checks and source references.\n\n## 9. Panel hash verification\n\nNo panel was rebuilt or changed. Only player identity, season and FTA columns were read for required accounting; measurement provenance was inspected separately without calculating any exposure/outcome association.\n\n| Panel | Seasons | Player-seasons | Players | FTA | 2013–14 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Primary replication | 13 | 4,117 | 857 | 469,099 | Excluded |\n| Full secondary | 14 | 4,428 | 866 | 511,686 | Included |\n\n- Primary SHA256: `{r['panels']['replication']['sha256']}`\n- Full SHA256: `{r['panels']['full']['sha256']}`\n\nBoth equal the original frozen hashes. `panel_release_receipt.json` points to these existing files. Historical candidate labels and pending source flags inside the unchanged files remain historical; the external Stage 3B receipt carries the new authorization.\n\n## 10. Part B authorization decision\n\n**{g['classification']}**; `part_b_authorized = true` in the new Stage 3B artifact only. The original execution-status file and Stage 3A decision are unchanged. Future Part B must cite the original failure, unresolved precision audit, prospective amendment, and amended re-release. Authorization permits future work; **Part B was not run in Stage 3B**. No hierarchical/beta-binomial model, correlation, posterior, OR, credible interval, effect plot or scientific direction was calculated.\n\n## 11. Frozen limitation language\n\n> {LIMITATION}\n\nThis exact language is frozen in both protocol and authorization and is required in all subsequent Stage 3 reports. The additional audit-scope and asymmetric-distribution qualifications above also remain relevant.\n\n## 12. Reproducibility\n\nInitial execution used the existing pinned Stage 3 Python environment, without installing dependencies:\n\n```sh\n.venv/bin/python scripts/stage3b_release.py freeze\n.venv/bin/python scripts/stage3b_release.py reassess\n.venv/bin/python scripts/stage3b_report.py\n.venv/bin/python scripts/verify_stage3b.py\n```\n\nThe freeze command refuses to overwrite the adopted protocol. Reassessment uses the same preserved observations and does not execute historical builders. The first release receipt is retained as the dated decision; offline review should run the verifier rather than replace its timestamps. The verifier checks A–J and additional source/limitation integrity, including counterfactual gate failures for every missing or false condition. Preauthorization inventory, protocol hash and ordered timestamps establish the local audit sequence. Absence of scientific outputs is checked against workspace filenames, preserved execution records and the explicit no-analysis workflow; no claim is made about artifacts outside this workspace.\n\n`test_run.txt`, `test_summary.json` and `build_manifest.json` record executed tests, environment and artifact hashes. No original FTM/FTA data, candidate files or historical decisions were modified. No commit or push was performed.\n'''
